+raised. Rules are compared based on their path, subdomain or host, websocket
+mode, and methods. Variable parts are not equal if they use different
+converters, although this heuristic may not be perfect depending on what the
+different converters can actually match. Rules with the same path are only
+duplicates if they share at least one method. A rule that does not specify
+``methods`` allows all methods, so it is a duplicate of any other rule with the
+same path.
+
+The path is compared after ``merge_slashes`` is applied, so ``/a//b`` is a
+duplicate of ``/a/b`` unless merging is disabled for that rule. A branch
+``/a/`` and a leaf ``/a`` are never duplicates, even if ``strict_slashes`` is
+disabled, as requests for each are routed to the rule that matches exactly.
 
 
